From 8b2abc77c170045d8e2ebb3ec5e4cbc0d184d77d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ducndh <ducndh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 03:20:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add GetDirectBlockPointer() for zero-copy block access

Add virtual BlockManager::GetDirectBlockPointer(block_id) that returns
a direct pointer to block data without going through BufferManager::Pin().

SingleFileBlockManager implements it by lazily mmap'ing the database file
(MAP_SHARED, read-only) and computing block offsets from the file layout.
Returns nullptr for writable, encrypted, or remote databases.

Eliminates Pin() overhead for read-only scans (470ms on SF100).
